From 6731fa98e36c4b0a6e198e3fe9d38d481bfa53e6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Micha=C5=82=20Kope=C4=87?= <michal.kopec@3mdeb.com>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 10:08:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 141/158] util/amdfwtool: record hash and license in generated
 SBOM tags
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The generated PSP firmware tags carried neither an integrity hash nor any
license information, so every AMD component appeared in the SBOM without
either. Record the SHA-256 of each firmware binary as a CoSWID payload file
hash (CRA Annex I integrity) and, when --sbom-license is given, a license
link (CRA Art. 13(5)).

These blobs have no SPDX license identifier, so the href is passed in
rather than hardcoded; it is meant to point at the redistribution terms
they are covered by. Both fields are omitted rather than emitted empty when
unavailable, so a missing binary or an unset license still yields a valid
tag.

amdfwtool already links libcrypto for signed_psp.c, so hashing adds no new
dependency. EVP_Digest()/EVP_EncodeBlock() are used in preference to the
deprecated one-shot SHA256() interface.

Change-Id: I118ec7b3d34f15164fdb2ca75566da5b89ceefcd
Signed-off-by: Michał Kopeć <michal.kopec@3mdeb.com>
(cherry picked from commit bae7b3925f3301efa24e2287b9c2c42f18e6110a)
